### D-21
date: 2026-10-10
milestone: M9
scope: extension
title: The sidebar adopts Google Calendar's own visual language and drops its title
question: Should the sidebar keep its own look (white card, "Weekly Pool" title, uppercase section labels, chip cloud), or match Google Calendar?
answer: Match Google, asked by the author on 2026-10-10 with three reference screenshots in `design-ref/`. Remove the "Weekly Pool" title. Borrow from Google's left nav (02) its surfaces, type and "My calendars"-style collapsible sections; from Google's event editor (03) its field vocabulary (grey pill fields, calendar dropdown with a colour dot, Notification row, "Does not repeat" select, filled blue pill buttons); and from the week view (01) the event chip, so a pool item looks like the event it creates. Prefer reading Google's live computed colours over hardcoding them, so both themes match exactly. Never depend on Google's class names; keep theme.ts's approach.
