### D-23
date: 2026-10-10
milestone: M9
scope: extension
title: The pool stays a separate sidebar; docking into Google's menu is not approved
question: Q-8: after the M9 U10 experiment, does the pool stay a separate sidebar or become part of Google's left nav?
answer: Separate sidebar (the author, 2026-10-10). Evidence from the real page: Google's "My calendars" is a div[role=list] of fixed height whose rows are each a div[role=presentation] pinned with transform: translateY(n×32px), so nothing inserted between rows gets room; nesting items under a calendar would mean rewriting Google's layout on every redraw. One section after the list would work but repeats the calendar names under Google's own. Hiding Google's list and drawing a copy was rejected: its failure mode breaks Google's own features (calendar toggles, the ⋮ menu). The dock code (aa690a0, e1c31d4) is removed in d303769; all three commits were dropped from history on 2026-10-13 (D-32), so those ids no longer resolve. Kept for later: each row carries data-id = base64 of the calendar id and --checkbox-color = its colour, a sturdier way than names to match Google's rows (e.g. for M9 U7's primary-calendar name).
supersedes: D-22
state: live

