### D-25
date: 2026-10-10
milestone: M7
scope: repo
title: Issues are welcome; pull requests are not accepted for now
question: On what terms do outside contributions come in, given AGPL-3.0-only (D-20)?
answer: Issues only (the author, 2026-10-10). CONTRIBUTING.md welcomes bug reports and ideas and says pull requests are closed without merging, so every line stays the author's and every licensing option stays open. Rejected: PRs under AGPL with inbound = outbound, which would need each contributor's consent to ever relicense; and a CLA-style grant, which deters contributors and wants a lawyer's wording. Loosening this later means a new decision and a new CONTRIBUTING.md.
state: live

### D-26
date: 2026-10-11
milestone: M8
scope: extension
title: The sidebar shows in Week and Day view only; every other view gets Google's layout back
question: The sidebar showed on every view, though placing worked only in Day and Week view. Which views should it work in?
answer: Week and Day view (the author, 2026-10-11; first week only, then Day added the same day because it cost nothing and a user whose default is Day would otherwise see nothing). Week counts with weekends shown or hidden; Month, Year, Schedule, the custom N-day view, Settings and the full event editor do not. Outside them the sidebar's mount is hidden, not unmounted, so a half-typed item survives, and Google's root loses the transform and width the sidebar gave it. The view is read from the path (/r/week, /r/day vs /r/month, …); a bare /r, which shows the user's default view, is read from the grid: 1 or 7 day columns, or Monday to Friday. Built in 4f93103.
state: live

### D-27
date: 2026-10-11
milestone: M7
scope: publishing
title: The extension is named Usuals; its slug is calendar-usuals
question: "\"Weekly Life Pool\" is disliked (\"pool\" says nothing). What is the product called, and may Google's name be part of it?"
answer: **Usuals** (the author, 2026-10-11), after "The Usuals" was dropped as sounding like a band. The premise it names: people have a set of usual actions, templates of what they do, kept under their calendars. Shown with the line "Works with Google Calendar" beneath it, never in the name: Google's brand guidance forbids its product names in a product name, OAuth brand verification rejects them, and "works with" is the phrasing Google itself permits; a line that Google Calendar is a trademark of Google LLC goes on the homepage and listing. The slug is **calendar-usuals**: the GitHub repository (github.com/kfireliyahu/calendar-usuals, M7 U5) and the homepage, kfireliyahu.com/calendar-usuals with /calendar-usuals/privacy (M7 U6). The OAuth consent screen's app name, the store listing's name and the homepage's title and heading all read exactly "Usuals", since verification compares them. Rejected after a clash check (web search only, no trademark register): Weekfill (weekfill.com, same idea), Slotted (slotted.com), Tray (Tray.ai), Regulars (Regularly planner app), Go-tos (GoTo), Stencils (Eventual Calendar's feature name). Nearest to Usuals: the iOS app Usual (household reminders) and usuals.app (contacts tool); a trademark search is still to do before launch.
state: live

### D-28
date: 2026-10-11
milestone: M10
scope: extension
title: Month view placing comes after launch, as all-day events that Shift repeats monthly
question: Should a usual be placeable in Month view, and when?
answer: Yes, after launch (the author, 2026-10-11). In Month view a drop, a click with an item picked, or the schedule form creates an all-day event on that date: no hour, no duration (the item's durationMin is ignored). Shift makes it repeat monthly. Month view is then added to the views the sidebar shows in (amends D-26); Year and Schedule stay hidden. Estimated at about a day: all-day event bodies and a monthly RRULE, a cell highlight and tooltip in place of the time-grid preview and placeholder, a month mode for click-to-place and the schedule form, and keeping drops off the mini month in Google's left nav. Not before launch because everything blocking launch is outside the code; it may be built while OAuth verification is pending. Left open: Q-9 (what monthly means), Q-10 (reminders on all-day events), Q-11 (Week view's all-day row).
state: live

