### D-3
date: 2026-09-06
milestone: M2
scope: extension
title: A pool drag carries two dataTransfer types, poolItem for the calendar and poolReorder for the sidebar
question: How can a sidebar drag reorder items without the document-level drop listener creating a calendar event, and vice versa?
answer: One drag sets both `poolItem` (read only by the document-level drop listener, which creates an event) and `poolReorder` (read only by the sidebar). Neither handler can pick up the other's payload, so one drag serves both targets. The document listener also only acts on `closest('[role="gridcell"]')`.
state: live

### D-30
date: 2026-10-11
milestone: M7
scope: repo
title: pool.emd is committed, in Emerald's text storage, once scrubbed; history rewritten a second time
question: D-12 kept pool.emd private and out of the repo. Should the project's plans and decisions travel with the code, and what has to go first?
answer: Committed (the author, 2026-10-11), so the project's memory is versioned with the code, the repository starting private (M7 U5). Before that: (1) a scan of pool.emd and the whole git history found the author's old personal address in src/names.ts comments (16 commits, added after D-19's rewrite) and, in pool.emd, that address, a private note and the old GitHub account's name. The comments now use made-up examples (pat@example.com, Pat Doe; c20424e); `git filter-repo --replace-text` removed the address from every commit, and the same run reworded the first two commit messages; no object in the repo holds it now. A backup bundle of the pre-rewrite history is at F:\projects\google-calendar-pool.before-usuals-rewrite.bundle, to be deleted once the new repository is checked. (2) The pool.emd rows were rewritten without those details, and every commit id they cite was mapped to the rewritten history (50 ids in 40 rows). (3) The file was stored as SQLite, whose free pages still held the deleted text; the author switched it to Emerald's text storage in the app, a scan of the text file came back clean, and only then was it committed. Backups (*.emd.*.bak, *.before-*.emd) stay ignored. Kept in it on purpose: me@kfireliyahu.com, the public name, the OAuth client ids and project number (public by nature), references to site.emd and Emerald.
supersedes: D-12
state: live

