### M8 U1
milestone: M8
scope: extension
title: chrome.storage.sync so the pool follows the user between machines
landed: 2026-10-09
state: built
brief: 0d5ab2e. Layout in `chrome.storage.sync`: `item:<id>` per item, `order:<calendarId>` id lists, `hiddenCategories`, `poolSchema: 1` (written only with real content). Per-item keys keep each under 8 KB and let two machines edit different items; cap ~500 items. Sidebar UI state stays local. Migration: unsynced local edits (`poolMirror`) > sync if `poolSchema` > one-time copy of old local `poolItems` (old keys left as backup). Writes coalesced (1.5 s idle, 10 s max, 5 s apart; flushed on hide). Size-quota errors → local-only with a once-per-page toast; rate errors retried in 60 s. `onChanged` merges per key, ignores echoes, keeps open forms. Items of calendars not in this account are now kept rather than deleted on save. Tested against a fake quota-enforcing chrome.storage (24 checks), not in Chrome.
files: `src/poolStore.ts` (new), `src/components/PoolSidebar.tsx`, `src/poolItem.ts`, `README.md`
taken_by: agent 4 (storage.sync), managed by the google-calendar-pool session
started: 2026-10-09

