### M8 U14
milestone: M8
scope: extension
title: drops land at the wrong hour when Google Calendar's time zone differs from the OS
landed: 2026-10-10
state: built
brief: 0b8aa21. Zone choice (`resolveCalendarZone`): the primary calendar's `timeZone` from calendarList if it agrees with the grid's `GMT±hh` gutter label (or no label is found); else the browser zone if it agrees; else the label as a fixed offset (`Etc/GMT∓N`, sign inverted, for whole hours); else the browser zone as before. "Agrees" = shows that offset within 7 days, because the label prints one offset per week. `wallToInstant` converts via Intl `formatToParts`, DST-safe. The schedule form's Today and default time use `calendarNow()`. Same-zone bodies proven byte-identical across every 15-min slot of 2026 in six browser zones. Unverified: the label finder on Google's real DOM, and whether the API accepts `Etc/GMT∓N`.
