brief: 307e70a. Export and Import buttons at the start of the sidebar footer (shown once the pool has loaded). src/poolTransfer.ts: buildExport writes {format: "usuals-export", version: 1, exportedAt, calendars: [{calendarId, name?, folded?, items}]} for every calendar the pool holds anything for, those of other accounts included, as usuals-YYYY-MM-DD.json (Blob + a[download], no new permission); parseExport rebuilds each item from PoolItem's fields only (id and name required, durationMin 1-1440, reminderMin 0-40320, colorId one of Google's 11, text fields non-blank), counts and skips the rest, and refuses a non-export or a newer version with a toast-worded ImportError. Decided: import only adds (merge by id), never replaces or overwrites, so importing twice changes nothing. poolStore.mergePool appends new ids at the end of their calendar's order, unions the folded calendars, writes through the mirror and sync flush, and notifies subscribePool listeners. loadPool now returns the current pool once loaded instead of the first reading's cached promise (also fixes M8 U19's quiet refresh reading stale storage). Toast: "Imported N usuals", plus how many are for calendars this account does not have (kept, not shown) and how many were unreadable. Format round-trip and validation checked with a node script; not driven in Chrome. README feature and structure, PRIVACY.md Your choices updated.
