brief: Found 2026-10-14 by the author with a fresh Google account whose Calendar Settings → Information density was "Comfortable" (theirs is "Responsive to your screen", which draws an hour 60 px tall). At Comfortable the hours are shorter, so no day column passed isTimeGridCell's 20 × 60 px floor: at a bare /r URL, where isWeekOrDayView reads the view from the grid, the sidebar never showed (switching to Day and back gave /r/week, which skips the grid read), and every drop said "Drop on a time slot". Fixed in d791710: calendarGrid.ts measures pixelsPerMinute from the day column's own height, which always spans midnight to midnight, and drop time, the drag preview and the loading placeholder in content.tsx all scale by it; the floor is now 24 × 16 px, still well over month cells and the all-day row. Tested by the author on their own account switched to Comfortable. Released as 0.1.1 (63ea416; release/usuals-0.1.1.zip, built by npm run package), submitted to the store by the author on 2026-10-14, **approved and published by 2026-10-15**; installed copies update themselves.
