### M9 U10
milestone: M9
scope: extension
title: experiment: the pool as a section inside Google's left nav
landed: 2026-10-10
decision: D-22
state: built
brief: Dropped from history on 2026-10-13 (D-32), so the ids in this brief no longer resolve. e1c31d4 (reworks aa690a0 at the author's request, 2026-10-10: items nest under each calendar's own row in Google's 'My calendars' instead of one 'Pool' section). Experiment behind a per-device flag, off by default (D-22): `dockInNav` in chrome.storage.local, same footer toggle; while ☰ is open and the rows are found, the separate sidebar hides and clearLayout gives the page its room back. Anchoring (dock.ts findAnchors): per calendar, the checkbox outside [role=main] and our own nodes whose accessible name (names.ts checkboxName) equals the calendar's name; climb to the first li/[role=listitem], else the last ancestor holding no other checkbox; believed only if shown and ≤64 px tall. No dependence on the 'My calendars' fold button. All-or-nothing: a calendar with items whose name is on no checkbox, on two, or shared by another pool calendar (duplicate names cannot be told apart) means no dock and the separate sidebar; calendars without items need no row (if found uniquely they still take dropped chips). All rows must share one parent (the list). List semantics: one container per calendar with items, placed as a sibling right after the row (not inside it: Google's row is a one-line, likely fixed-height flex box whose content Google re-renders); it is an li when the row is an li, role=listitem when the row has that role, so the list stays a list of items; inside, a fold button (count + chevron, aria-expanded, name 'N items in the pool for <calendar>') and a ul labelled 'Pool items for <calendar>'. Fold reuses the synced hiddenCategories (U3). Indent measured from the checkbox's offset (fallback 32 px), ~200 px chips; tokens via .wlp-dock-host in content.css, theme kept by applyTheme. One React root: every container and the bar are portals. Re-render: one MutationObserver on body, callback skips [role=main], our nodes, tooltip/preview, then schedules one check per animation frame (before paint, so no flicker); the check verifies rows/containers/bar in place and only then re-searches and re-places everything in one pass, keeping the same host elements (focus restored). Budget: passes <1 s apart are one redraw episode (Google may draw a list in steps); >8 re-placings within one episode = fight, or >20 episodes per minute = give up for the page (retry by switching the flag on again); rows gone (e.g. Google folds 'My calendars') = sidebar meanwhile, looks again 5 s. Popover (DockPopover, in the sidebar mount, 280 px, fixed, beside the chip, below it if no room): role=dialog, focus moves in (ScheduleForm autofocus, details' location, composer title), Escape or Tab past either end closes and returns focus to the opener, outside press closes; a press on the grid while picked still places (content script's capture handler runs first). Composer: '+ New item' quiet text button once in a bar after the list (with toasts and the switch), opening the composer in the popover — not a '+' on Google's rows (collides with the ⋮), and present even when no calendar has items. Drag: grid drops never check the drag's origin (confirmed: content.tsx reads poolItem + gridcell under pointer), Shift-drop, click-to-place, rename, reorder within a list, move by dragging onto another calendar's nested list or onto its Google row (document capture listener + calendarAtRow; index 0). Removed: findMyCalendars/TOGGLE_SELECTOR, #wlp-dock, the 'Pool' header and fold, dockFolded; sidebar tree restored to pre-aa690a0 markup plus the switch. Default-path changes (all no-ops with the flag off): renderItem/composerForm/toastRegion extracted (verified identical markup when not docked), names.ts outsideSidebar also skips .wlp-dock-host, applyTheme queries .wlp-dock-host, nav-change focus check also looks in dock hosts. Keep/drop is the author's after a day of use: keep if no lost drops, no layout fights, no console errors; drop if it needs class names, flickers, or is too narrow — then Q-8 is answered 'separate sidebar'. Verified: tsc, build, and 26 checks of dock.ts against a mock nav in Chromium (virtual clock): anchoring, duplicate/missing rules, li/listitem/div rows, aria-labelledby names, redraw and move re-placement with the same hosts, refresh on fill/empty, hidden list → fallback and back, fight → give-up, spaced redraws keep docking. Unverified: nothing ran in Chrome against Google Calendar — whether Google's rows are li/listitem and ≤64 px, whether its renderer removes foreign siblings on every draw (then it gives up), whether its list is a plain stacked flow (a virtualized/absolute list would overlap), the real indent and width, drag start inside the nav and the off-screen drag image, row drops, the popover's position and keyboard flow, theme switch, RTL pages, screen-reader output.
