brief: 156f2b9. Surface: theme.ts gained `detectSurface(theme)` and a `PageLook {theme, surface}`; `watchTheme` now calls back with both and re-applies when either changes. The surface is read by walking from `[role="banner"]` (else <body>) up to the first background with alpha >= 0.5; it is used only if fully opaque and its luminance agrees with the theme, else null. content.tsx sets it on the sidebar mount as inline `--wlp-page`; content.css `--wlp-surface: var(--wlp-page, #f8fafd)` light / `var(--wlp-page, #1f1f1f)` dark. Sidebar's right border removed. `--wlp-hover` is now `color-mix(text 8%, transparent)` in both themes (translucent state layer). Dark `--wlp-pill` is now `color-mix(text 12%, var(--wlp-surface))` (~#373737 on the fallback) instead of the remembered #37393b; light pill stays #fff. Type/spacing tokens on `#weekly-life-pool-sidebar`: `--wlp-font` ('Google Sans', Roboto, Arial, sans-serif), `--wlp-type-name` 14px, `--wlp-type-section` 16px, `--wlp-weight-section` 500, `--wlp-row-height` 32px, `--wlp-gutter` 16px. `.wlp-sidebar` uses the font and 14px base. Applied: `.wlp-item` min-height 32px, padding 0 12px, 14px (text-[13px] removed; rename input 14px too), list gap 4px; `.wlp-cat-header` min-height 40px, padding 4px gutter; new `.wlp-cat-title` (16/500, --wlp-text, sentence case, truncate) on the category h3, replacing the 11px uppercase label (design choice: the brief's ~16px medium section titles made uppercase untenable, so U3 inherits sentence case already done; U3 still owns chevron/collapse, folding hide/show, empty sections). Form, hidden strip, footer and "No calendars found" use the 16px gutter. Scrollbar: `.wlp-scroll` on the category list, `scrollbar-width: thin`, thumb `--wlp-scrollbar` (text at 24% light / 30% dark) shown only on :hover / :focus-within, transparent track. Note Tailwind/Lightning CSS emits color-mix custom properties inside `@supports (color: color-mix(in lab, red, red))` with a `var(--wlp-text)` fallback before it; fine in Chrome. Unverified: not loaded in Chrome; whether Google Calendar has a `[role=banner]` whose ancestor chain paints the page colour (else the constants stand in); the actual sampled colour in light and dark; thin scrollbar width on Windows and the hover reveal; 16px titles and 32px rows at 280px width; the translucent hover over fields in the schedule/details panels.
