### M9 U8
milestone: M9
scope: extension
title: the sidebar fits the viewport and coexists with Google's own nav
landed: 2026-10-10
decision: D-21
state: built
brief: edceff7. Clipping: the sidebar was `height: 100vh`, which counts a horizontal scrollbar along the bottom of the window as page; the shifted Google root (translateX + narrowed width) can overflow to the right and give the page one, so the column ran ~15 px below the visible area (matches the footer cut at y≈933 in 01). Fix: the sidebar is held by `top:0; bottom:0` (a fixed box's insets exclude scrollbars), Google's root gets `overflow-x: clip` (clip, not hidden, so it is no scroll container and sticky headers still work), and the column is `.wlp-column` (flex 1 1 0, min-height 0) with header/footer flex-shrink 0, the list `.wlp-list` (flex 1 1 0, min-height 0, scrolls), and the composer allowed to shrink and scroll inside itself once its open animation ends (formSettled), for windows under ~330 px. Nav: the default sidebar steps aside to its 40 px strip while Google's main menu is open and comes back when it closes. Reason: Google's nav (256 px) takes nearly the room the pool gives up (240 px), so the week keeps its width and the two transitions compose instead of squeezing the grid twice; one side panel at a time, as Google's own side panels are. The auto-collapse is never saved; opening the pool from the strip while the menu is open keeps it beside the menu until the menu next changes. Detection is geometry, not ARIA: `layout.ts` measures the root's start edge to `[role=main]`'s start edge (>=120 px = open), re-read at most once a frame from a ResizeObserver on main, window resize and any click; no class names or translated labels. Layout code moved from content.tsx to new `src/layout.ts`; content.tsx no longer shifts the page from storage at load, the sidebar dispatches the shown width once (avoids a 280-then-40 jiggle). Keyboard: hiding/showing (by click or by the menu) moves focus to the toggle that replaces the removed one, only if focus was actually lost. RTL page (`dir=rtl` body): sidebar stays physically left with mount `dir=ltr` (its words are English; tooltip too), root is narrowed but translated by 0, since a narrowed start-aligned root already sits against the right edge; nav measured from the right edge. Mirroring the sidebar to the right in RTL was considered and left for later (chevrons, toasts, bidi of English strings). For U10: the nav watcher is `watchGoogleNav` in layout.ts; a docked mode should bypass the auto-collapse and adjustLayout, and its result answers Q-8. Unverified: not loaded in Chrome, so the scrollbar diagnosis, that [role=main] excludes Google's nav (if it includes it, the pool never steps aside, harmlessly), that Google's root sits flush right in RTL, and both themes are untested.
